# --------------------------------------------------
# Generic attributes and settings for the repository.
#
# Define general file handling and cross-platform behavior using native
# Git attributes here. Keep project, framework, external-tool, and
# hosting-service rules in appropriately scoped .gitattributes files.
#
# Text rules control line ending normalization. Binary rules disable text
# normalization, text diffs, and automatic text merges. Named diff drivers
# below use Git's built-in patterns.
#
# Explicit text and eol attributes take precedence over core.autocrlf.
# Rules below use LF by default and define CRLF exceptions where needed.
# Changing attributes does not rewrite existing files or automatically
# renormalize the index.
#
# A leading / anchors a pattern to the directory containing this file.
# A trailing / does not apply attributes to a directory's descendants. Use /**
# instead. Patterns without a leading or middle slash match names at any depth
# below this file. The last matching rule wins per attribute within a file,
# while a nested .gitattributes takes precedence for its subtree.
#
# Match a filename at any depth:    CODEOWNERS
# Match a root-level file:         /CODEOWNERS
# Match a specific path:           .github/CODEOWNERS
# Match a directory's descendants: media/**
# Match a file type at any depth:  *.json
#
# Negative patterns (!pattern) are not supported.
#
# Use export-ignore for files that should be omitted from Git source archives.
# Keep archive exclusions specific to the project's distribution needs.
#
# For more information, see:
# https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes#_end_of_line_conversion
# https://github.com/gitattributes/gitattributes
# --------------------------------------------------

# --------------------------
# Common Rules
# --------------------------

# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
*           text=auto eol=lf

# Text files where line endings should be preserved
*.[dD][iI][fF][fF]                  -text
*.[pP][aA][tT][cC][hH]              -text

# Ignore files
*.*[iI][gG][nN][oO][rR][eE]         text      eol=lf

# Scripts
*.[pP][sS]1                         text=auto eol=lf
*.[bB][aA][tT]                      text      eol=crlf
*.[cC][mM][dD]                      text      eol=crlf
*.[bB][aA][sS][hH]                  text      eol=lf
*.[fF][iI][sS][hH]                  text      eol=lf
*.[kK][sS][hH]                      text      eol=lf
